## Test Strategy Components

- **Load Testing**: Simulate realistic user traffic patterns with gradual ramp-up
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement request throttling and batching to respect API limits
- **Error Handling**: Test retry mechanisms with exponential backoff and circuit breakers
- **Contract Testing**: Validate API responses against schemas and documentation
- **Monitoring**: Track performance metrics, error rates, and system resource utilization

## Tools & Implementation

```javascript
// Example retry logic with exponential backoff
const retryRequest = async (url, retries = 3) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      const response = await fetch(url);
      if (response.ok) return response;

      // Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s
      const delay = Math.pow(2, i) * 1000;
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
    } catch (error) {
      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;
    }
  }
};

// Rate limiting implementation
class RateLimiter {
  constructor(maxRequests = 100, timeWindow = 60000) {
    this.maxRequests = maxRequests;
    this.timeWindow = timeWindow;
    this.requests = [];
  }

  async makeRequest(requestFn) {
    const now = Date.now();
    this.requests = this.requests.filter(time => now - time < this.timeWindow);

    if (this.requests.length >= this.maxRequests) {
      const waitTime = this.timeWindow - (now - this.requests[0]);
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, waitTime));
    }

    this.requests.push(now);
    return await requestFn();
  }
}
```

## Testing Phases

1. **Baseline Testing**: Establish performance metrics under normal load
2. **Stress Testing**: Identify breaking points and failure modes
3. **Spike Testing**: Test sudden traffic increases and recovery
4. **Endurance Testing**: Validate performance over extended periods
5. **Rate Limit Testing**: Verify behavior at and beyond rate limits
